{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>ומחיר</b> Two times in the Masorah: ומחיר כלב and ומחיר שדה עתודים. This is what they said: he gave her wheat and she made it into fine flour — and this is ומחיר שדה. And similarly עתודים also, for he exchanged a lamb for a dog." "<b>כי תועבת ה' אלהיך גם שניהם</b> And adjacent to it: לא תשיך — to say that both the lender and the borrower and the guarantor are abhorrent."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The rabbinic dictum referenced appears in b. Bava Metzia 64b, concerning one who lends wheat on condition to be repaid in fine flour. Ba'al HaTurim reads both Masorah occurrences of ומחיר as alluding to prohibited exchange-for-interest scenarios.", 1 "The word גם שניהם (both of them) is read as encompassing not only the two parties named in context but three parties; the adjacency of לא תשיך (Deut. 23:20) supplies the linkage to the broader prohibition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:30.897429403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}